# XSH atomic_flag_clear(), atomic_flag_clear_explicit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The state of a flag can only be observed with atomic_flag_test_and_set(),
# so these tests use it; setup checks on it are UNRESOLVED if they fail.

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_clear.001
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_clear.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After atomic_flag_clear() on a set flag, atomic_flag_test_and_set()
           returns false, and sets the flag again (repeated five times).
test       t/001-clear.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_clear.002
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_clear.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_flag_clear_explicit() with memory_order_relaxed, _release
           and _seq_cst (the orders allowed for it) clears a set flag, also
           when called repeatedly on a clear one.
test       t/002-clear-explicit-orders.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_clear.003
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_clear.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       Clearing a clear flag leaves it clear (plain and explicit forms);
           clearing one flag of an array leaves the other four set.
test       t/003-clear-isolated.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_clear.004
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_clear.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.15.1
class      required
since      2024
says       Ordinary data written before atomic_flag_clear_explicit(release) is
           visible to a thread whose atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit
           (acquire) then returns false, over 2000 hand-offs.
note       A stalled hand-off (20 s) is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/004-clear-release-handoff.c
